Catppuccin themes for Ableton Live

Catppuccin Mocha.ask and Catppuccin Latte.ask come from the Wires Ableton
Live 12 distribution, which ships them in its files/support/ folder together
with a copy of the LGPL-2.1 licence text (files/support/LICENCE.ableton-linux,
byte-identical to shibco/ableton-linux's LICENCE). Wires lists the themes in
the same support set as that licence file and carries no other licence,
notice or attribution for them, so they are redistributed here under
LGPL-2.1, whose text is in the LICENSE file next to this notice.

The Wires runtime credits the project's maintainers for its contents:

    Cade Diehm
    Lucas Gillingham
    Wires, built on https://github.com/shibco/ableton-linux

These files are not part of this repository's GPL-3.0 work and are not
relicensed under it. They are aggregated alongside it under their own terms:
keep this NOTICE and LICENSE with them when you copy or redistribute them.

The Catppuccin colour palette is by the Catppuccin contributors and is
released under the MIT licence (https://github.com/catppuccin/catppuccin).
The themes are an adaptation of that palette for Live's theme format; their
colour values are not copied from the upstream project, so the credit here
is a courtesy rather than a licence condition.

Wires also ships "Catppuccin Auto.ask", which is byte-identical to
"Catppuccin Mocha.ask" (SHA-256 61de4018...) and therefore does not follow
the system light/dark setting. It is not included in this folder.
